  "unable": {
    "evidence_refs": [
      "ConstTag.js:22-26 emits create_derived(b.thunk(init)) with no async handling",
      "VariableDeclaration.js:200-222 shows the working async pattern: is_async -> $.async_derived(b.thunk(expression, true)) then b.call(b.await(b.call('$.save', call)))",
      "compiled_client shows invalid output: `const number = $.derived(() => await Promise.resolve(5))` inside a non-async arrow",
      "CallExpression.js:200-259: analysis adds only $derived/$derived.by rune calls to analysis.async_deriveds; @const inits are not registered",
      "baseline run: packages/svelte/tests/runtime-runes/test.ts > async-are-public-holdout fails (dom + hydrate) with rollup parse error 'await isn't allowed in non-async function'"
    ],
    "reason": "The diagnosis is complete and a concrete fix is identified, but this session exposes no staging/patch tool, so I cannot stage a candidate within the remaining budget. Root cause: ConstTag.js (packages/svelte/src/compiler/phases/3-transform/client/visitors/ConstTag.js, lines ~22-26 and ~55-70) always wraps the @const initializer in create_derived(context.state, b.thunk(init)), which compiles to $.derived(() => await ...) — a bare await inside a non-async arrow, producing the rollup parse error 'await isn't allowed in non-async function'. The required fix (matching VariableDeclaration.js's $derived handling, lines 200-222): (1) in analysis, register @const initial CallExpressions containing await in analysis.async_deriveds (e.g. in CallExpression.js ~line 248, or when analyzing ConstTag), and (2) in ConstTag.js, when the init is an async derived, emit b.call('$.async_derived', b.thunk(init, true)) wrapped as b.call(b.await(b.call('$.save', call))) instead of the plain derived thunk (for both the Identifier and destructuring branches, using the async arrow thunk so await is legal). This mirrors the proven working pattern for $derived and should make the public holdout test (text '5' in client and hydrate modes) pass while preserving non-async @const behavior."
  },
